{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover","id":1010716,"title":"Soul Loss and Crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T11:15:10-08:00","id":1010716,"title":"Soul Loss and Crossover","content":"What happens to the following splats when targeted with an effect that leads to soul loss? I'll be editing this OP to include various conjectures.<br /> <br /> <b>Speculative</b><br /> Vampires - Can lose their souls to Diablerie, which normally requires killing them. Probably suffers Soul Loss normally.<br /> Werewolves - Possibly suffers Soulless normally. If the soul is replaced with a different soul, they suffer the persistent Madness condition.<br /> Prometheans - If their soul analog <i>is</i> removed, you're probably looking at a Firestorm<br /> Changelings - Their powers stem from what's left of their Soul being infused with Wyrd. I'd treat it similarly to Mages<br /> Sin-Eaters - Their soul is merged with their Geist. Probably unremovable.<br /> Demons - Don't have souls. Possibly suffer a Compromise when it would have been lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Confirmed.</b><br /> Humans and Hunters - Suffer Soulless.<br /> Beasts - Die.<br /> Mummies - Immune to Soul Loss, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-30-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:26:01-08:00","id":1010723,"title":"","content":"With Prometheans, their &quot;soul&quot; is a mote of Divine Fire, so I assume ripping it out would ignite a Firestorm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:49:07-08:00","id":1010732,"title":"","content":"If you ripped the human soul, a Beast would probably go on a Hunger-frenzy, either in the dreamscape or even in the physical world<br /> <br /> Probably a similar thing would happen to Sin-Eaters. With the body being left entirely to the control of the Geist. Whether that's good, bad or neutral depends on the Geist involved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:01:13-08:00","id":1010744,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd imagine that Werewolves would become an Empty Wolf. Idigam can tear out their souls and replace them with other souls, or with Spirits, creating powerful Claimed with the body and natural abilities of the Uratha. If another soul, or a Spirit, isn't inserted into the Werewolf, I'd imagine they keep all the usual stuff, but they can't learn new Gifts or Facets, nor can they gain new Renown brands.<br /> <br /> I think they'd experience the Soulless Condition normally, but you'd have to decide if Blood or Bone leads more towards Spirit or Flesh in order to calculate to which extreme they experience Breaking Points towards. I <i>think </i>the Werewolf would need to hit Harmony 1 to reach Eneverated, but I've never run a Soulless Werewolf. Would they lose Primal Urge at all from falling Willpower? I don't think they should, since that's explicitly a Mage thing due to the fact that their power stems from an Awakened Soul and Will. When they hit Thrall I doubt the Werewolf would gain the Broken Condition, but maybe they'd have the Madness Condition instead? With its dice penalty applied to resisting Kuruth?<br /> <br /> One of the Unchained would probably become one of the Burned, unless they had another Cover as a backup. So, that means the Hunted Condition and the Blown Condition. It also means they might react, violently, in their newly exposed Demonic Form towards whoever took their Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:02:06-08:00","id":1010746,"title":"","content":"Beasts die. It's in the book.<br /> <br /> Or I thought it was. Tried to find a reference but I couldn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:21:55-08:00","id":1010760,"title":"","content":"Well, if the <i>Horror </i>dies they do. I think there was a reference back in the old Kickstarter versions of Beast, when the Nightmare &quot;You Are Meat&quot; was still a power you could get. But I figure there's a more interesting answer than 'they die' available. Maybe a Beast subject to the Soulless Condition starts hemorrhaging Satiety? They start regaining Willpower like a Hero (one point from Life, all from Legend) and indulging Legend means losing a point of Satiety. Eventually, they'd hit Ravenous and go on a horrendous rampage, if they didn't succumb to rage and despair and undergo the Merger before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:25:10-08:00","id":1010761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010760#post1010760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if the <i>Horror </i>dies they do. I think there was a reference back in the old Kickstarter versions of Beast, when the Nightmare &quot;You Are Meat&quot; was still a power you could get. But I figure there's a more interesting answer than 'they die' available. Maybe a Beast subject to the Soulless Condition starts hemorrhaging Satiety? They start regaining Willpower like a Hero (one point from Life, all from Legend) and indulging Legend means losing a point of Satiety. Eventually, they'd hit Ravenous and go on a horrendous rampage, if they didn't succumb to rage and despair and undergo the Merger before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the problem is that the Horror <i>is</i> the Beast's Soul. It's not like a Sin-Eater/Geist situation where one's riding the other. I get that &quot;And then they died&quot; can be boring, but it's also not <i>easy</i> to inflict Beasts with a Soulless Condition. I think they even say they're immune to most ways (pre-Archmastery Supernal magic, Demons, etc...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:26:00-08:00","id":1010762,"title":"","content":"Vampires do not suffer soul loss by effects that normally cause soul loss in humans in the VtR core book.<br /> <br /> I'll be a bit boring and say that it's probably the same for all non-human/Mage splats that don't have their own rules for dealing with soul loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:29:32-08:00","id":1010763,"title":"","content":"For Demon, I'd lean towards &quot;they aren't human and never were, so they don't have a soul to steal.&quot; Partly for continuity with oWoD where the Fallen were explicitly immune to soul loss, I think that's a good trait for a demon to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:41:07-08:00","id":1010770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010763#post1010763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Demon, I'd lean towards &quot;they aren't human and never were, so they don't have a soul to steal.&quot; Partly for continuity with oWoD where the Fallen were explicitly immune to soul loss, I think that's a good trait for a demon to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably have a Demon make a Compromise roll instead of suffering actual Soul Loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:51:27-08:00","id":1010773,"title":"","content":"Beasts have a goetia instead of a soul. If a mage tries to remove it using Death, nothing happens because it's the wrong arcarnum and they need to use Mind. <br /> <br /> I have no idea what happens if they actually manage to get it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:52:16-08:00","id":1010800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010762#post1010762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires do not suffer soul loss by effects that normally cause soul loss in humans in the VtR core book.<br /> <br /> I'll be a bit boring and say that it's probably the same for all non-human/Mage splats that don't have their own rules for dealing with soul loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accurate, though not the most exciting answer. However, many splats have implications of how soullessness might affect them - it's just caused by other means. Werewolves, for example, can have their souls removed by Idigam, which turns them into Su'Ur. The sidebar in Requiem about Solace suggests that the drug returne them to life for one night, and could be read as implying that it does so by rendering them (temporarily?) soulless.<br /> <br /> Prometheans don't have Souls yet, so I don't think there's any question that soul removing effects simply don't work on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:58:18-08:00","id":1010803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010773#post1010773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have a goetia instead of a soul. If a mage tries to remove it using Death, nothing happens because it's the wrong arcarnum and they need to use Mind.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what happens if they actually manage to get it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not only wrong, but Beasts' corebook clearly says what happens. The mage has to use Death 5, but mages <i>can</i> steal Beasts' souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:08:29-08:00","id":1010808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010800#post1010800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves, for example, can have their souls removed by Idigam, which turns them into Su'Ur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Su'ur are only created when an idigam replaces said soul with a spirit. If the soul is replaced with another soul, they gain a Persistent Madness Condition, as on p219, 'If it replaces the werewolf\u2019s soul with a spirit, this immediately creates an Empty Wolf, a unique type of Claimed that retains some of the Uratha\u2019s supernatural abilities. If the idigam does this with a soul, the werewolf suffers the persistent Madness Condition.'<br /> <br /> Considering the ability is Forge Empty Wolf, and refers specifically to taking a werewolf's soul and replacing it, it doesn't seem like an idigam can just take the soul out and leave it empty. At least not using that ability. Or, if so, it doesn't create anything special except a werewolf with the Soulless Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:14:15-08:00","id":1010810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010808#post1010808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, Su'ur are only created when an idigam replaces said soul with a spirit. If the soul is replaced with another soul, they gain a Persistent Madness Condition, as on p219, 'If it replaces the werewolf\u2019s soul with a spirit, this immediately creates an Empty Wolf, a unique type of Claimed that retains some of the Uratha\u2019s supernatural abilities. If the idigam does this with a soul, the werewolf suffers the persistent Madness Condition.'<br /> <br /> Considering the ability is Forge Empty Wolf, and refers specifically to taking a werewolf's soul and replacing it, it doesn't seem like an idigam can just take the soul out and leave it empty. At least not using that ability. Or, if so, it doesn't create anything special except a werewolf with the Soulless Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhmm, that's right. Sorry, I misremembered how that worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:51:49-08:00","id":1010835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010803#post1010803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not only wrong, but Beasts' corebook clearly says what happens. The mage has to use Death 5, but mages <i>can</i> steal Beasts' souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I found the bit in the book where it says how they get it out (and I would argue I was sort of <i>half</i> right. Just casting a spell in the material does indeed do nothing, because they need to be in the Lair, which is in the astral, which does funny things to arcarnum requirements.)<br /> <br /> But I can't find anything that says what happens to the Beast if it's taken. The soul loss condition just talks about integrity, virtues and vices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:13:12-08:00","id":1010924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1010835#post1010835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I can't find anything that says what happens to the Beast if it's taken. The soul loss condition just talks about integrity, virtues and vices.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror's death means the Beast's death, it explicitly can't be compelled to leave the Lair for any reason other than to hunt, the lasting detachment of the Horror from the Lair is normally part of an irreversible and fatal Inheritance claim, and and &quot;as much ability with the Arcana as taking the soul of a mage&quot; means &quot;Mastery of the Arcanum of Death.&quot;<br /> <br /> The implication seems pretty clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:29:00-08:00","id":1010939,"title":"","content":"I've edited OP to include some of this conjecture. Anyone have any input on what might happen to a Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:57:30-08:00","id":1011003,"title":"","content":"So let's see: The Primordial monster cloaked in humanity die when someone manages to rip away the nightmare-monster that is its soul from the nightmarish landscape that is also part of its soul. The hungry dead's true soul or equivalent may be it's inner Beast, not the inner Human. Removing the proto-soul of a (semi-)living alchemical furnace that also functions as its core is likely to result in a meltdown. Half-spirit scions of the God of the Hunt usually go mad when their soul is stolen, but we don't know if that's the general case or a special case where ancient alien gods are involved. And autonomous programs gone rogue from the world-wide network of occult symbols of The System don't have a soul, or count as a soul themselves.<br /> <br /> Any speculations for the Fog Men and Nameless weapons of mass destruction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T05:40:45-08:00","id":1011027,"title":"","content":"I already gave mine for the Fog Men. I think it basically turns them into Wretched who quickly lose the battle and give up the their body to their Geist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:39:56-08:00","id":1011043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011027#post1011027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already gave mine for the Fog Men. I think it basically turns them into Wretched who quickly lose the battle and give up the their body to their Geist</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like the Geist may actually be bonded to the Sin-Eater's soul, though, so yanking the soul might yank all or part of the Geist, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T09:09:04-08:00","id":1011106,"title":"","content":"My general rule is that the soul of supernatural critters, if it exists, is very different than those of humans, so why would removing it have the same effect?<br /> <br /> Werewolves, vampires, Changelings, mummies... All had souls once, but they were changed dramatically. They can't be removed like a mortal's because they don't have one anymore.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, Demons... They never had one to begin with. Nothing there to remove.<br /> <br /> Beast, meanwhile, is what happens when you remove the soul of a game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:14:10-08:00","id":1011126,"title":"","content":"Huh... what would happen if you actually did remove the soul (and thereby, the horror) from a beast and then swapped it out with someone else's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:44:52-08:00","id":1011133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011106#post1011106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves, <b>vampires</b>, Changelings, mummies... All had souls once, but they were changed dramatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the consensus was that the soul did... whatever souls do at death, and the Beast filled the original soul-socket.<br /> <br /> ...that said, it's just an impression, I can't recall if it was actually spelled out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:28:05-08:00","id":1011152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011133#post1011133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the consensus was that the soul did... whatever souls do at death, and the Beast filled the original soul-socket.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast seems to entwine itself with the vampire's soul, keeping it from escaping. Vampires do have their souls, it's just not alone there, similar to most other games. Changeling souls are torn up, with Fae magic filling the holes, Werewolf souls are made part-hunter spirit, Sin-Eater souls part ghost. <br /> <br /> The idea that you are replaced by the Beast was a thought-experiment by someone reacting to 'Would you be a vampire if you could.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-02-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:10:59-08:00","id":1011160,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as strongly as I feel that &quot;the Beast replaces you&quot; doesn't make any observable difference, I do think it's important to stress that it is <i>not</i> the default assumption. Vampires definitely have souls in Requiem as-writte , though their souls are evidently altered by the Embrace in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:46:51-08:00","id":1011539,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined that the Soul was definitely altered when someone was embraced, but I imagine that if you rip the soul out of a vampire only the Beast remains; I don't imagine ripping out a vampire's soul would leave them anything more than a Draugr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:43:56-08:00","id":1011567,"title":"","content":"I thought there was something left of the soul in the Draugr though. Otherwise, why would the Strix still find them too human if they were purely the Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:49:01-08:00","id":1011571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011539#post1011539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always imagined that the Soul was definitely altered when someone was embraced, but I imagine that if you rip the soul out of a vampire only the Beast remains; I don't imagine ripping out a vampire's soul would leave them anything more than a Draugr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Diablerie is said to be one vampire consuming another vampire's soul. So the best information we have is that removing a vampire's soul causes Final Death. Lending further credence to this interpretation is the fact that Stirges can Diablerize humans via Breath Drinking, and doing so leaves the human with the Soulless Condition. Stirges also can't use Breath Drinking on vampires, because their Vitae is said to be too bound up in their blood to be extracted through breath. The same could be true of their souls; spells that remove or destroy souls don't work on vampires, not because they don't have souls, but because their souls cannot be separated from their blood. But if you do drain all of a vampire's blood first and then remove her soul, she dies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011567#post1011567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there was something left of the soul in the Draugr though. Otherwise, why would the Strix still find them too human if they were purely the Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and Draugur can be Diablerized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-03-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:53:11-08:00","id":1011574,"title":"","content":"Sort of off-topic, but with all this talk about the vampire's, well, everything, seems to reside in their blood, has anyone thought of seeing if transplanting all of the blood of one vampire into a drained corpse would transfer his consciousness to that body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:01:49-08:00","id":1011581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011574#post1011574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of off-topic, but with all this talk about the vampire's, well, everything, seems to reside in their blood, has anyone thought of seeing if transplanting all of the blood of one vampire into a drained corpse would transfer his consciousness to that body?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would. Vampires can survive being completely drained of Vitae, it just causes them to fall into Torpor. It's only exsanguinating them <i>and then continuing to drink anyway</i> that kills them, and when that happens, the Diablerist does hear the victim's thoughts in her mind, at least for a little while. Eventually the Tainted Condition fades as the weaker soul is consumed by the stronger one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:57:03-08:00","id":1011743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1010716-soul-loss-and-crossover?p=1011581#post1011581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it would. Vampires can survive being completely drained of Vitae, it just causes them to fall into Torpor. It's only exsanguinating them <i>and then continuing to drink anyway</i> that kills them, and when that happens, the Diablerist does hear the victim's thoughts in her mind, at least for a little while. Eventually the Tainted Condition fades as the weaker soul is consumed by the stronger one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair, but what if one drained somebody, and then pumped the sludge of a macerated whole vampire into their veins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:03:42-08:00","id":1011746,"title":"","content":"You can't really surgically drain Vitae, it doesn't flow through their veins to be drained. Another vampire could do it, or with magic somehow.<br /> <br /> But if a vampire gave up all their Vitae somehow, or it was magically drained, and you injected it into your veins, you would probably suffer some of the affects of imbibing Vitae and the vampire would be very hungry.<br /> <br /> A vampire's consciousness is not confined to their Vitae. Though vampire magic could easily justify a vampire that transfers themselves that way, it would be a benefit of the ability, not the Vitae itself.<br /> <br /> I think there is one, among one of the more religious bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-03-2016, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}